# Jmix Security Rules

## Scope
Applies to `src/main/java/**/security/`

## Resource Role Pattern
```java
@ResourceRole(name = "Role Name", code = RoleName.CODE)
public interface RoleName {
    String CODE = "role-code";
    
    @EntityPolicy(entityClass = Entity.class, actions = EntityPolicyAction.ALL)
    @EntityAttributePolicy(entityClass = Entity.class, attributes = "*", action = EntityAttributePolicyAction.MODIFY)
    void entity();
    
    @ViewPolicy(viewIds = {"Entity.list", "Entity.detail"})
    void views();
    
    @MenuPolicy(menuIds = {"Entity.list"})
    void menu();
}
```

## Policies
- `@EntityPolicy` — CRUD operations
- `@EntityAttributePolicy` — Attribute access (MODIFY/VIEW/HIDE)
- `@ViewPolicy` — Screen access
- `@MenuPolicy` — Menu item visibility
- `@SpecificPolicy` — Custom permissions

## Row-Level Security
- `@RowLevelRole` + `@JpqlRowLevelPolicy`
- Use `{E}` for entity alias
- Variables: `:current_user_username`

## Forbidden
- Hardcoded passwords/secrets
- Bypassing security checks
- Missing entity policies for views
